# Hari OS — example environment file
#
# Copy to `.env.local` if you need to override anything locally:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local` is git-ignored and must never be committed. This file is tracked
# and must never contain real secrets or machine-specific paths.
#
# Hari OS V1 runs on localhost with no deployment, so this file is currently
# short. Variables are added here only when code actually reads them.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HARI_OS_DB_PATH
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Leave unset for normal local development.
#
# By default the SQLite database lives at:
#
#   data/hari-os.db
#
# resolved relative to the project root. The directory and file are created
# automatically on first use, so nothing needs to be created by hand.
#
# Set this only to point the app at a different database, for example a
# throwaway file used while testing:
#
#   HARI_OS_DB_PATH=data/hari-os.test.db
#
# A relative value is resolved from the current working directory. Do not
# commit a real local path here, and do not use this to point at a shared or
# production database — V1 has no deployment and no remote database.
